      "content": "I'm a bit confused by your comparison. Please don't use metaphors; I need this to be strictly professional as this is for a client. \n\nRegarding the human-driven disruptions: if a period of civil unrest occurs that was not explicitly listed in the lease agreement, does the \"foreseeability\" test still allow the court to interpret it under a general force majeure clause, or must the specific type of event be enumerated in the contract for it to be valid in Singapore?",
